trition Information for Cardiovascular Disease Prevention: Cross-Sectional Study#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)":[33,35],"#Evaluating Large Language Models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation Enhancement for Delivering Guideline-Adherent Nutrition Information for Cardiovascular Disease Prevention: Cross-Sectional Study#🟡 Genel Bilgiler (Sarı)#{1}":[34,35],"#Evaluating Large Language Models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation Enhancement for Delivering Guideline-Adherent Nutrition Information for Cardiovascular Disease Prevention: Cross-Sectional Study#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)":[36,38],"#Evaluating Large Language Models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation Enhancement for Delivering Guideline-Adherent Nutrition Information for Cardiovascular Disease Prevention: Cross-Sectional Study#🟢 Yöntem & Örneklem (Yeşil)#{1}":[37,38],"#Evaluating Large Language Models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation Enhancement for Delivering Guideline-Adherent Nutrition Information for Cardiovascular Disease Prevention: Cross-Sectional Study#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[39,41],"#Evaluating Large Language Models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation Enhancement for Delivering Guideline-Adherent Nutrition Information for Cardiovascular Disease Prevention: Cross-Sectional Study#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[40,41],"#Evaluating Large Language Models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation Enhancement for Delivering Guideline-Adherent Nutrition Information for Cardiovascular Disease Prevention: Cross-Sectional Study#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[42,44],"#Evaluating Large Language Models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation Enhancement for Delivering Guideline-Adherent Nutrition Information for Cardiovascular Disease Prevention: Cross-Sectional Study#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[43,44],"#Evaluating Large Language Models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation Enhancement for Delivering Guideline-Adherent Nutrition Information for Cardiovascular Disease Prevention: Cross-Sectional Study#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[45,46]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/3KRQ99DY","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/8BSYEVV3?page=1&annotation=AEIMQZZ5","line":34},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/8BSYEVV3?page=1&annotation=T59LDPU2","line":37},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/8BSYEVV3?page=2&annotation=FFNAYFP8","line":40},{"title":"Sayfa 10","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/8BSYEVV3?page=10&annotation=7YWHH8KS","line":43},{"title":"Sayfa 2","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/8BSYEVV3?page=2&annotation=97KYQCFE","line":43}],"metadata":{"Title":"Evaluating Large Language Models and Retrieval-Augmented Generation Enhancement for Delivering Guideline-Adherent Nutrition Information for Cardiovascular Disease Prevention: Cross-Sectional Study","Authors":"Vijaya Parameswaran, Jenna Bernard, Alec Bernard, Neil Deo, Sean Tsung, Kalle Lyytinen, Christopher Sharp, Fatima Rodriguez, David J Maron, Rajesh Dash","Year":2025,"DOI":"10.2196/78625","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"We curated 30 nutrition questions that comprehensively addressed CVD prevention. These were approved by a registered dietitian providing preventive cardiology services at an academic medical center and were posed 3 times to each model.  We developed a 15,074-word knowledge bank incorporating the American Heart Association’s 2021 dietary guidelines and related website content to enhance Meta’s Llama 3-70B model using RAG. The model received this and a few-shot prompt as context, included citations in a Context Source section, and used vector similarity to align responses with guideline content, with the temperature parameter set to 0.5 to enhance consistency.","Findings":"The Llama 3+RAG model scored higher than the Perplexity, GPT-4o, and Llama 3 models on reliability, appropriateness, guideline adherence, and readability and showed no harm. The Cohen coefficient ( >70%; P<.001) indicated high reviewer agreemen","Conclusions":"The off-the-shelf models scored lower on all measures and produced some harmful responses. These findings highlight the limitations of off-the-shelf models and demonstrate that RAG system integration can enhance LLM performance in delivering evidence-based dietary information.Our cross-sectional study evaluating LLM responses to common nutrition questions demonstrated that the RAG-enhanced Llama 3 model grounded in CV dietary guidelines consistently outperformed 3 off-the-shelf models (ChatGPT-4o, Perplexity, and Llama 3-70B) by providing more appropriate, reliable, and guideline-adherent responses to common nutrition questions with no evidence of harm, although these responses were less readable due to their technical language. In contrast, the off-the-shelf models scored lower on all measures and produced harmful content. These findings highlight the limitations of off-the-shelf models and demonstrate that RAG enhancement can improve LLM performance in delivering evidence-based dietary informati","Limitations":"","User_Notes":"prompt var  yanıt da var  klinik değ var karşılaştırma yok"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"cteptj","at":1774939668115}},"smart_blocks:parameswaranEvaluatingLargeLanguage2025b.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.0863869,0.03405173,0.02697234,0.0276226,0.0425354,-0.00095372,-0.06259555,0.05802538,0.01248865,-0.02457675,0.01874932,-0.11647858,0.05011869,0.02890484,0.07435234,0.00255741,0.03807809,0.04561418,-0.02343773,0.0342541,0.06031453,-0.02001329,0.04080988,-0.01110878,0.07842422,0.01058137,-0.02292782,-0.01369608,-0.07198193,-0.24699917,0.02642479,-0.01861749,0.05881005,-0.02919604,-0.08120355,0.013669,0.01032898,0.03679173,-0.02172364,0.0398639,0.01876263,0.03575645,0.04209904,-0.01293671,-0.02678092,-0.0382322,-0.037